<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $177.9 mln Dec 2.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $177.9 mln Dec 2.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $177.9 million surplus on December 2 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 2</p>
<p>Exports: $244.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $118 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $160.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $109.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $177.9 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
</text>
